tps://linkedin.com/in/obahamondem/details/certifications/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-d359282e>LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div><a class="text-link" href="https://linkedin.com/in/obahamondem/details/certifications/">Ver credenciales en LinkedIn<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></section><section id="blog" data-section class="section shell"><div class="section-heading numbered-heading" data-number="07" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">07 / IDEAS EN ABIERTO</p><h2>Notas desde<br><span>la ingeniería.</span></h2></div><p>Artículos sobre software, datos e inteligencia artificial. Publicados originalmente en Medium.</p></div><div data-v-67e762ef><div class="blog-grid" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><article class="blog-card" lang="es" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/quipubase-una-base-de-datos-semantica-inspirada-en-el-quipu-andino-5a4fecfd18c7" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><div class="editorial-cover" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><span data-v-67e762ef>openai</span><strong data-v-67e762ef>Quipubase: Una base de datos semántica inspirada en el quipu andino</strong><small data-v-67e762ef>Oscar Bahamonde · Medium</small></div></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2025-08-04T08:33:37.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>4 ago. 2025</time><span data-v-67e762ef>ES</span><span data-v-67e762ef>3 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/quipubase-una-base-de-datos-semantica-inspirada-en-el-quipu-andino-5a4fecfd18c7" class="" data-v-67e762ef>Quipubase: Una base de datos semántica inspirada en el quipu andino</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>“El futuro de los datos puede aprender del pasado.” Vivimos en una era donde los datos están en todas partes: APIs, bases vectoriales, LLMs, flujos JSON, modelos multimodales… pero ¿y si pensáramos nuestras estructuras de datos como redes vivas, narrativas, jerárquicas y culturalmente conscientes? De esa intuición nace Quipubase , una plataforma documental y semántica…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>openai</span><span data-v-67e762ef>ai</span><span data-v-67e762ef>database</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://medium.com/@obahamonde/quipubase-una-base-de-datos-sem%C3%A1ntica-inspirada-en-el-quipu-andino-5a4fecfd18c7" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><article class="blog-card" lang="en" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/openai-in-a-box-oss-technical-design-of-the-silicon-valley-behemoth-1b0754aaace6" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><img width="640" height="390" data-nuxt-img sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 33vw" srcset="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 1w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 2w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 338w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 384w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 676w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 768w" onerror="this.setAttribute(&#39;data-error&#39;, 1)" alt loading="lazy" class="blog-image" src="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F800%2F1*nLa0ochLpabYj8tW675G8w.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85" data-v-67e762ef></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2025-04-05T05:46:02.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>5 abr. 2025</time><span data-v-67e762ef>EN</span><span data-v-67e762ef>5 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/openai-in-a-box-oss-technical-design-of-the-silicon-valley-behemoth-1b0754aaace6" class="" data-v-67e762ef>OpenAI In a Box: OSS Technical Design of the Silicon Valley Behemoth</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>🌟 Overview OpenAI In a Box is an enterprise-grade, open-source implementation of the OpenAI-compatible API architecture, engineered to deploy seamlessly on AWS infrastructure while supporting the full spectrum of generative AI endpoints. This project delivers a self-hosted, horizontally scalable solution designed for organizations that require sovereign AI infrastructure with performance comparable to leading commercial providers.…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>deployment</span><span data-v-67e762ef>model</span><span data-v-67e762ef>infrastructure</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://python.plainenglish.io/openai-in-a-box-oss-technical-design-of-the-silicon-valley-behemoth-1b0754aaace6" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><article class="blog-card" lang="en" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/memory-safety-meets-performance-the-power-of-modern-programming-languages-22943f84d25a" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><div class="editorial-cover" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><span data-v-67e762ef>programming-languages</span><strong data-v-67e762ef>Memory Safety Meets Performance: The Power of Modern Programming Languages</strong><small data-v-67e762ef>Oscar Bahamonde · Medium</small></div></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2025-03-26T04:45:41.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>26 mar. 2025</time><span data-v-67e762ef>EN</span><span data-v-67e762ef>3 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/memory-safety-meets-performance-the-power-of-modern-programming-languages-22943f84d25a" class="" data-v-67e762ef>Memory Safety Meets Performance: The Power of Modern Programming Languages</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>In the world of programming, the eternal quest for balance between performance and safety has led to the development of numerous languages, each with its own strengths and weaknesses. However, one language has been making waves in recent years with its unique approach to memory management, offering the best of both worlds: high-level simplicity with…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>programming-languages</span><span data-v-67e762ef>memory-safety</span><span data-v-67e762ef>performance</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://medium.com/@obahamonde/memory-safety-meets-performance-the-power-of-modern-programming-languages-22943f84d25a" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><article class="blog-card" lang="es" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/evaluacion-comparativa-chatgpt-vs-llama-3-para-empresas-y-creadores-de-contenido-3d729d316f13" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><div class="editorial-cover" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><span data-v-67e762ef>ai</span><strong data-v-67e762ef>Evaluación Comparativa: ChatGPT vs Llama 3 para Empresas y Creadores de Contenido</strong><small data-v-67e762ef>Oscar Bahamonde · Medium</small></div></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2024-12-14T11:21:26.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>14 dic. 2024</time><span data-v-67e762ef>ES</span><span data-v-67e762ef>2 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/evaluacion-comparativa-chatgpt-vs-llama-3-para-empresas-y-creadores-de-contenido-3d729d316f13" class="" data-v-67e762ef>Evaluación Comparativa: ChatGPT vs Llama 3 para Empresas y Creadores de Contenido</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>En un mundo donde la IA se vuelve cada vez más crucial para el trabajo intelectual, realizamos un análisis exhaustivo de dos modelos líderes: ChatGPT y Llama 3. El objetivo: determinar sus fortalezas y casos de uso óptimos. Metodología Desarrollamos un test de 10 preguntas enfocadas en: - Análisis estratégico - Resolución de problemas -…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>ai</span><span data-v-67e762ef>llama-3</span><span data-v-67e762ef>chatgpt</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://medium.com/@obahamonde/evaluaci%C3%B3n-comparativa-chatgpt-vs-llama-3-para-empresas-y-creadores-de-contenido-3d729d316f13" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><article class="blog-card" lang="en" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/genai-101-building-a-streaming-responses-chatbot-with-openai-client-gradio-and-g-e8fd267e2375" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><img width="640" height="390" data-nuxt-img sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 33vw" srcset="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 1w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 2w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 338w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 384w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 676w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 768w" onerror="this.setAttribute(&#39;data-error&#39;, 1)" alt loading="lazy" class="blog-image" src="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F0*Oo2Eg8nbl_MbfzGs&amp;w=768&amp;q=85" data-v-67e762ef></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2024-11-07T05:37:23.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>7 nov. 2024</time><span data-v-67e762ef>EN</span><span data-v-67e762ef>3 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/genai-101-building-a-streaming-responses-chatbot-with-openai-client-gradio-and-g-e8fd267e2375" class="" data-v-67e762ef>[GenAI 101] Building a Streaming Responses Chatbot with OpenAI client, Gradio and Groq.</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>Welcome to “GenAI from Zero to Hero” — your guide to mastering Generative AI technologies! In this tutorial, we’ll create a real-time streaming chatbot using OpenAI Client on Groq API and Gradio to compose a rich UI. Introduction Chatbots have transformed how we interact with technology, offering instant support and engaging user experiences. Today, we’ll…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>large-language-models</span><span data-v-67e762ef>python</span><span data-v-67e762ef>artificial-intelligence</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://blog.gopenai.com/genai-101-building-a-streaming-responses-chatbot-with-openai-client-gradio-and-groq-e8fd267e2375" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><article class="blog-card" lang="en" data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/introduction-to-language-model-merging-2e88b80e190b" class="" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-v-67e762ef><img width="640" height="390" data-nuxt-img sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 33vw" srcset="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 1w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 2w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 338w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=640&amp;q=85 384w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 676w, /_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85 768w" onerror="this.setAttribute(&#39;data-error&#39;, 1)" alt loading="lazy" class="blog-image" src="/_vercel/image?url=https:%2F%2Fcdn-images-1.medium.com%2Fmax%2F1024%2F1*w-Jz28URZgk65h-pkMY6Mw.png&amp;w=768&amp;q=85" data-v-67e762ef></a><div class="post-meta" data-v-67e762ef><time datetime="2024-08-18T19:14:35.000Z" data-v-67e762ef>18 ago. 2024</time><span data-v-67e762ef>EN</span><span data-v-67e762ef>4 min</span></div><h3 data-v-67e762ef><a href="/es/blog/introduction-to-language-model-merging-2e88b80e190b" class="" data-v-67e762ef>Introduction to Language Model Merging</a></h3><p data-v-67e762ef>Language model merging is a next-level technique that combines multiple pretrained language models (LLMs) into a single, more powerful, and efficient model. This approach is a game-changer, allowing you to supercharge your models without the hassle of retraining from scratch, saving both time and compute — because who has time for that? Why Merge Models?…</p><div class="post-tags" data-v-67e762ef><!--[--><span data-v-67e762ef>technology</span><span data-v-67e762ef>ai</span><span data-v-67e762ef>llama-3</span><!--]--></div><a class="text-link" href="https://ai.plainenglish.io/introduction-to-language-model-merging-2e88b80e190b" data-v-67e762ef>Leer en Medium<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></article><!--]--></div><div class="feed-footer" data-v-67e762ef><!----><!----><button class="button" data-v-67e762ef>Cargar más artículos<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-down-icon" data-v-67e762ef><path d="M12 5v14"></path><path d="m19 12-7 7-7-7"></path></svg></button><p class="fineprint" data-v-67e762ef>6 / 10 · Artículos disponibles en el RSS</p></div></div></section><section id="contact" data-section class="section section-tint contact-section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading numbered-heading" data-number="08" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">08 / EMPECEMOS UNA CONVERSACIÓN</p><h2>Tu próxima idea<br><span>empieza aquí.</span></h2></div><p>Cuéntame qué quieres construir o reserva una sesión para resolver una duda concreta.</p></div><div class="contact-grid"><div class="assistant-invitation spotlight-card"><div class="invitation-orbit" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="58" height="58" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-bot-icon"><path d="M12 8V4H8"></path><rect width="16" height="12" x="4" y="8" rx="2"></rect><path d="M2 14h2"></path><path d="M20 14h2"></path><path d="M15 13v2"></path><path d="M9 13v2"></path></svg><span>AI</span></div><p class="eyebrow">UNA IDEA ES UN BUEN COMIENZO</p><h3>Conversemos sobre lo que viene.</h3><p>Explora servicios, tecnologías y posibilidades con mi asistente de IA. A tu ritmo, en tu idioma.</p><button class="button primary magnetic" type="button">Hablar con el asistente<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></button><span class="fineprint">O reserva una conversación conmigo.</span></div><article class="booking-card"><div class="booking-heading"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-calendar-days-icon"><path d="M8 2v4"></path><path d="M16 2v4"></path><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2"></rect><path d="M3 10h18"></path><path d="M8 14h.01"></path><path d="M12 14h.01"></path><path d="M16 14h.01"></path><path d="M8 18h.01"></path><path d="M12 18h.01"></path><path d="M16 18h.01"></path></svg><span class="mono">1:1 / CONSULTING</span></div><h3>Una conversación. Un siguiente paso.</h3><div class="booking-price">S/20<span>30 minutos · Google Meet</span></div><p class="fineprint">Lunes a viernes · 09:00–13:00 y 14:00–17:00 · Lima (UTC−5)</p><div class="booking-flow"><p class="eyebrow">1 · Elige tu horario</p><label for="meeting-date">Fecha · hora de Lima (UTC−5)</label><input id="meeting-date" value="2026-11-14" type="date" min="2026-11-14"><p role="status">No hay espacios disponibles para este día. Prueba otra fecha.</p><!----><!----><p class="fineprint booking-note">Retenemos el horario 15 minutos para completar el pago seguro en MercadoPago. Al aprobarse, confirmamos la cita y enviamos la invitación de Calendar con Google Meet. Sin pago, el espacio vuelve a estar disponible.</p></div></article></div><div class="contact-social"><span>También puedes escribirme</span><a href="mailto:oscar.bahamonde.dev@gmail.com">oscar.bahamonde.dev@gmail.com <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right-icon"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="https://github.com/bahamondex">GitHub bahamondex</a><a href="https://github.com/obahamonde">GitHub obahamonde</a><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/obahamondem/">LinkedIn</a><a href="https://medium.com/@obahamonde">Medium</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="footer shell"><div><span class="footer-name">Oscar Bahamonde<span class="accent-dot">.</span></span><p>Software con propósito. Ingeniería con criterio.</p></div><div class="footer-bottom"><small>© 2026 Oscar Bahamonde · Perú</small><a href="/es/privacy" class="">Privacidad</a><a href="https://medium.com/@obahamonde">Medium ↗</a><a href="mailto:oscar.bahamonde.dev@gmail.com">Email ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="dock-wrap" aria-label="Explorar el portafolio"><ul class="dock"><!--[--><li class="dock-item" style="--magnify:1;"><a aria-current="location" href="/es#home" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active dock-link dock-home" aria-label="Inicio"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="25" height="